Patch @vanillagreen/pi-tool-renderer so only a tool call that started executing
blinks while it is pending.

Pi keeps a tool call pending until a result arrives: ToolExecutionComponent
starts with executionStarted false and isPartial true, and only a result clears
them. A turn aborted between the call and its result therefore leaves a card
that stays pending forever, and the blink timer invalidates it every 450ms for
the rest of the session. In regular TUI mode a transcript longer than the
screen puts that card above the visible viewport, where pi-tui cannot patch a
frame incrementally and falls back to a full redraw that erases the terminal
scrollback (tui-main-screen.ts, "\x1b[2J\x1b[H\x1b[3J"). The result is a
transcript that repaints twice a second and cannot be scrolled.

Gating the blink on executionStarted keeps the animation for calls that are
actually running, since only those can finish and stop it.

Applied by flake/packages.nix after npm install. To apply it to a development
checkout, run from the repository root:

  patch -p1 -d node_modules/@vanillagreen/pi-tool-renderer < patches/pi-tool-renderer-pending-blink.patch

Upstream: github.com/vanillagreencom/kendex

--- a/extensions/tool-renderer/text.ts
+++ b/extensions/tool-renderer/text.ts
@@ -188,7 +188,12 @@
 }
 
 export function pendingStatusPrefix(theme: any, context: any, cwd?: string): string {
-	if (pendingStatusAnimation(context?.cwd ?? cwd)) return blinkingPrefix(theme, context, cwd);
+	// A call that never started executing can never finish, so blinking it only
+	// invalidates frames for the rest of the session. In regular mode each of
+	// those repaints clears the terminal scrollback.
+	if (context?.executionStarted && pendingStatusAnimation(context?.cwd ?? cwd)) {
+		return blinkingPrefix(theme, context, cwd);
+	}
 	clearBlink(context);
 	return theme.fg("warning", glyphs(context?.cwd ?? cwd).bullet);
 }
